{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician upon Muthlabben, A Psalm of David. I will praise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", O LORD, with my whole heart; I will show forth all thy wonderful works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou most High.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When my enemies are turned back, they shall fall and perish at thy presence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou hast maintained my right and my cause; thou sattest on the throne judging right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast rebuked the heathen, thou hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast put out their name for ever and ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O thou enemy, destructions are come to a perpetual end: and thou hast destroyed cities; their memorial hath perished with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the LORD shall endure for ever: he hath prepared his throne for judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the people in uprightness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee: for thou, LORD, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sing praises to the LORD, who dwelleth in Zion: declare among the people his doings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he maketh inquisition for blood, he remembereth them: he forgetteth not the cry of the humble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have mercy upon me, O LORD; consider my trouble ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which I suffer",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from them that hate me, thou that liftest me up from the gates of death:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That I may show forth all thy praise in the gates of the daughter of Zion: I will rejoice in thy salvation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heathen are sunk down in the pit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they made: in the net which they hid is their own foot taken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD is known ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he executeth: the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands. Higgaion. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked shall be turned into hell, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all the nations that forget God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the needy shall not always be forgotten: the expectation of the poor shall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perish for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, O LORD; let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged in thy sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.9.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.9.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Put them in fear, O LORD: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the nations may know themselves ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " men. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
